==============================================================================
PART A1 -- the field, stated explicitly
==============================================================================
  F_4 = F_2[w]/(w^2 + w + 1);  w^2 = w + 1;  w^3 = 1
  encoding: a0 + a1*w  ->  a0 + 2*a1
      0=0  1=1  w=2  w^2=3
  addition table (^):
      0  1  2  3
      1  0  3  2
      2  3  0  1
      3  2  1  0
  multiplication table:
      0  0  0  0
      0  1  2  3
      0  2  3  1
      0  3  1  2
  multiplicative order of each unit: 1:1, w:3, w^2:3

==============================================================================
PART A2 -- the code C = <1+x> in F_4[x]/(x^3 - 1)
==============================================================================
  g(x) = 1 + x  (degree 1)
  |C| = 16   dim_F4 C = 2
  C is 1-constacyclic (closed under T_1): True
  C is w-constacyclic: False ;  w^2-constacyclic: False
  all codewords (weight in brackets):
     ('0', '0', '0')  [0]
     ('0', '1', '1')  [2]
     ('0', 'w', 'w')  [2]
     ('0', 'w^2', 'w^2')  [2]
     ('1', '0', '1')  [2]
     ('1', '1', '0')  [2]
     ('1', 'w', 'w^2')  [3]
     ('1', 'w^2', 'w')  [3]
     ('w', '0', 'w')  [2]
     ('w', '1', 'w^2')  [3]
     ('w', 'w', '0')  [2]
     ('w', 'w^2', '1')  [3]
     ('w^2', '0', 'w^2')  [2]
     ('w^2', '1', 'w')  [3]
     ('w^2', 'w', '1')  [3]
     ('w^2', 'w^2', '0')  [2]
  weight distribution of C: {0: 1, 2: 9, 3: 6}

==============================================================================
PART A3 -- the monomial map phi = diag(1, w, w^2), i.e. f(x) -> f(w x)
==============================================================================
  diag(1,w,w^2) equals f(x) -> f(wx) on every element of the ring: True
  phi is diagonal with nonzero entries => preserves every Hamming weight
  |phi(C)| = 16   dim_F4 = 2
  phi(C) is 1-constacyclic (closed under T_1): True
  phi(C) is w-constacyclic: False
  all codewords of phi(C):
     ('0', '0', '0')  [0]
     ('0', '1', 'w')  [2]
     ('0', 'w', 'w^2')  [2]
     ('0', 'w^2', '1')  [2]
     ('1', '0', 'w^2')  [2]
     ('1', '1', '1')  [3]
     ('1', 'w', '0')  [2]
     ('1', 'w^2', 'w')  [3]
     ('w', '0', '1')  [2]
     ('w', '1', 'w^2')  [3]
     ('w', 'w', 'w')  [3]
     ('w', 'w^2', '0')  [2]
     ('w^2', '0', 'w')  [2]
     ('w^2', '1', '0')  [2]
     ('w^2', 'w', '1')  [3]
     ('w^2', 'w^2', 'w^2')  [3]
  weight distribution of phi(C): {0: 1, 2: 9, 3: 6}
  identical weight distributions: True
  C == phi(C) as sets: False

